{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 — the COLLECTION ground only (collection WINNING-SPEC §3.1). Mirrors
  snippets/elmsnest-v2-ground-product.liquid, which does the same job for the PDP, and
  snippets/elmsnest-v2-ground-index.liquid, which does it for the homepage.

  Rendered by sections/elmsnest-v2-coll-scene.liquid ONLY, once per page, at the very top of its
  markup — exactly as the hero renders elmsnest-v2-ground-index and the stage renders
  elmsnest-v2-ground-product. No other section may render it; rendering it twice would print the
  same <style id> twice for no gain.

  The page-agnostic tokens / type / lamps / buttons live in snippets/elmsnest-v2-core.liquid, which
  layout/theme.liquid renders on EVERY template. Nothing here redefines a core token, nothing here is
  per-instance, so there is no Liquid below the comment.

  THE ONE IDEA (§3.1): a collection page's length is unknown — 6 products is one screen, 27 is five.
  A percentage-stop gradient would therefore put "deep night" at 30 % of a short page and at 78 % of a
  long one, and the two pages would not look like the same shop. So the sky is measured in PIXELS: every
  collection reaches full night at the same distance from the top and then simply stays there.

  Specificity note (load-bearing, same trap as the PDP ground): elmsnest-v2-core sets the generic
  side-page ground with `body[class*="hdt-page-type-"]:not(.hdt-page-type-index)` = (0,2,1). A plain
  `body.hdt-page-type-collection` is (0,1,1) and would LOSE, so every rule here is written
  `html body.hdt-page-type-collection…` = (0,2,2). Everything is scoped to that class, so no other
  template — index, product, page, search, cart — can be touched by this file.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style id="env2-ground-collection">
/* ---------- page ground (§3.1): night measured in px, not % ----------
   Screen 1 is a photo ground painted by elmsnest-v2-coll-scene; the document below it is this one
   gradient and nothing else. No section paints a background (§3.1: the only card surface anywhere on
   this page is the scrim --env2-scrim + backdrop-filter, used exactly twice). */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection{
  background-color:#020306;
  background-image:linear-gradient(180deg,
    #0f1a2f 0px,
    #0d1626 900px,
    #0a1120 2200px,
    #080e1c 3800px,
    #060a14 5600px,
    #04070e 7600px,
    #020306 9800px);
  background-repeat:no-repeat;
  background-size:100% 100%;
  background-attachment:scroll;
  min-height:100vh;
}
/* A page that is SHORTER than the gradient (6 products, one screen) must not be handed a squashed
   sky: background-size:100% 100% would compress the ramp into a 2000px document and the short page
   would go black three times faster than the long one. Painting the ramp on a fixed box anchored at
   the top and letting #020306 fill the rest keeps every collection identical for its whole length,
   which is the whole point of §3.1.
   CREATIVE-05 — the ramp used to be spent by 5,000px, so from there down every collection was one
   flat near-black field: 5,700px of it on decor and 13,700px on /collections/all, which is most of
   the page and reads as "nothing here" rather than as night. It now runs to 9,800px — decor's whole
   length, and past the ruler, the bands, the ladder and the ledger on every URL — and it starts at
   --env2-sky-2 (#0f1a2f), which is the colour the scene's veil lands on, so the photograph still
   joins the ground with no seam. (The critic asked for --env2-sky-1 at the top; that would put a
   visible step across the foot of the hero on all five URLs, because the veil's own last stop is
   sky-2. The descent it asked for is delivered by the length of the ramp, not by its first stop.) */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection{background-size:100% 9800px}
/* ---------- CREATIVE-07: the unlit lamp must still read as a photograph ----------
   The core's dim floor is brightness .22 / saturate .4, and on this page it is not a rare state: a
   visitor who follows the page's own in-page anchors (#env2-coll-ruler, #env2-coll-terms) lands past
   every card between here and there, and the observer never sees them — 45 of 63 lamps on
   /collections/all and 8 of 17 on decor stay dim for the rest of the session. At .22 a warm garden
   photograph measures mean luminance 18/255 with a standard deviation under 1: a featureless brown
   blur under a live 'הוספה לסל' button, which reads as a broken image, not as a lamp waiting to be
   lit. The floor is raised here — on the collection page only, so the homepage and the product page
   keep the core's own value — and the switch-on gesture is kept: .52 -> .90 is still a visible
   lighting, and the accompanying halo, pool and glow layers are untouched.
   CREATIVE-03 also rides on this: at .90/.92 the lit state carries a little less of a studio frame's
   daylight, which the bands' multiply veil then finishes. */
body.hdt-page-type-collection [data-lamp] .env2-ph img{
  filter:brightness(calc(.52 + .38*var(--lit,1))) saturate(calc(.72 + .2*var(--lit,1)))}

/* Kalles wraps the template in painted containers; the sky must be visible between sections. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection #wrapper,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .main-content,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection main,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection #MainContent,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-main-content,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-page-content,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .shopify-section{background:transparent}
/* The header is transparent over the scene: the scene is the first section, starts at top 0 and clears
   the 70px bar with its own padding (§4.1). Kill any inherited gap above it — Kalles ships a top margin
   on the first collection section for its taupe banner, which this template retires (§5.4). */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection #MainContent>.shopify-section:first-child,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-main-content>.shopify-section:first-child{margin-block-start:0;padding-block-start:0}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection #MainContent>.shopify-section:first-child .env2-section,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-main-content>.shopify-section:first-child .env2-section{margin-block-start:0}
/* No horizontal page scroll at 360px (§6.13). The scene, the band scenes and the goodnight photo are
   full-bleed, and the ruler's dot rails scroll INSIDE their own row — never the document. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection{overflow-x:hidden}
/* §3.2's tap-target floor, on this template only. elmsnest-v2-core sizes .env2-btn--sm at 36px tall on
   desktop (it was sized for the PDP related row) and only raises it to 44px under 900px. The collection
   spec asks for 48px, 44px absolute, with no viewport caveat — so the floor is set here, scoped to the
   collection body, and the PDP is not touched. Measured in the plumbing render: 36px -> 44px. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-btn--sm{min-block-size:44px}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-pdp-card__action .env2-btn{min-block-size:44px}
/* §3.2's 13px floor for an information-bearing caption, same belt, same scope. The shared
   .env2-price__from is .62em, so on the ruler row and the ledger row (17px prices) the "מ־" that turns
   an exact price into a MINIMUM was measured at 10.54px — under the floor. elmsnest-v2-pdp-card already
   floors it inside its own price column; this does the same for every other price on this template. The
   selector is (0,2,2) and only sizes the shared class, it does not restyle it. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-price__from{font-size:max(13px,.62em)}
/* §6.13's 44px tap floor for every product-name link on this template. A one-line name is 21-22px and a
   two-line name is 43px, both under the floor; the hit area is expanded with padding that the negative
   margin gives straight back, so the vertical rhythm of every row is unchanged and only the touch box
   grows. sections/elmsnest-v2-coll-bands.liquid already does this for its own cards row; this belt adds
   the ruler row's name, the span ladder's name, the card title wherever a card is used, and the scene's
   own "to the ruler" link, which is a standalone link and not a link inside a sentence. Scoped to
   .env2-coll so no Kalles link and no PDP card is touched. 14px, not 12px: at 12px the scene's own
   19px-tall link came out 43px, one pixel short of the floor. Measured at 390 after the change: the
   scene link 19px -> 47px, a one-line name 21px -> 49px, a two-line name 43px -> 71px. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll .env2-pdp-card__title a,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll .env2-coll-ruler__title a,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll .env2-coll-span__name a,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll .env2-coll-scene__next a{display:inline-block;padding-block:14px;margin-block:-14px}
/* ---------- CREATIVE-04 + TYPOGRAPHER-05 / -06: the page's vertical rhythm and two row measures ----
   These six declarations belong to four sections that needed no other change this round
   (elmsnest-v2-coll-span, -ledger, -terms, -goodnight). They are kept here, page-scoped at (0,3,1),
   for the same reason the four belts above are: one place to read the collection page's spacing
   decision, one place to revert it. The ruler and the bands carry the identical values inside their
   own stylesheets because those two files were being rewritten anyway. The lead may fold the six
   into their sections in a later round; the values, not the location, are the finding.

   CREATIVE-04 — the page spent 216px of ground at every section boundary and ran long strings of
   2–4% ink screens against the homepage's 28.9% median. The spend is cut by about a third at every
   boundary. Nothing is removed but ground.
   TYPOGRAPHER-06 — inside one 56px ledger row the name ended at x 890 and its price started at
   x 100: ~710px of empty ground between a thing and its price. The terms row had ~300px gaps on
   both sides of one statement. Both are capped so the pairing survives at 1440.
   TYPOGRAPHER-05 — the fourteen measures are tabular figures but were start-aligned, so 9.5 put its
   9 where 10 puts its 1 and the מ׳ floated to a different x on every row. The numeral takes a fixed
   cell aligned on its end edge and the unit takes its own, so both form real columns. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-span{padding-block:clamp(56px,5.6vw,84px) clamp(40px,4.2vw,64px)}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-ledger{padding-block:clamp(56px,5.6vw,84px) clamp(40px,4.2vw,64px)}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-terms{padding-block:84px 64px}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-goodnight{padding-block:clamp(72px,7.6vw,108px) 44px}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-ledger__rows{max-inline-size:min(100%,960px)}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-terms__head,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-terms__ledger{max-inline-size:min(100%,1120px)}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-ledger__k{display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:clamp(46px,4.6vw,68px) auto;justify-content:start;align-items:baseline;gap:5px}
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .env2-coll-ledger__k>bdi{display:block;text-align:end}

/* Kalles' collection chrome that §5.4 retires from templates/collection.json. The section files stay on
   the theme until the owner signs off, so nothing is deleted; these two belts only make sure that a
   left-over instance cannot paint a cream strip or a taupe banner over the night. */
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-collection-toolbar,
html body.hdt-page-type-collection .hdt-collection-banner{background:transparent}
</style>
